  "body": "Part of #372 (option 2: the machine's axis really moves the other way). Shows an inverted machine axis (#373) wherever the operator reads the setup.\n\n## What changed\n- **Viewport triad** (`crates/ui/src/axis_note.rs`, hooked into `interact::overlay_labels`): the arrows stay the right-handed program frame (ISO 841); an inverted linear axis of the shown setup's machine gets a note label just under its letter, in the axis colour: `Machine X+ moves left (inverted axis)`. Drawn once (first triad), never by flipping the arrow (that would draw a left-handed frame the toolpaths are not in).\n- **Setup sheet** (`setup_sheet/sections.rs`): a `MACHINE AXES` section after the datum/alignment block, one line per inverted axis of the setup's own machine: `Machine X+ moves left (inverted axis) - the program is mirrored in X for this machine`.\n- **NC header**: `script_props` now publishes `machine.invertedAxes` (`[]` for standard machines); `fanuc.cps` and `haas.cps` (the only posts with `axisInversion = true`) write `(MACHINE X+ MOVES LEFT - INVERTED AXIS)` per axis right after the program-name line. All other posts refuse an inverted machine before their script runs (#374 `post::invert::apply`), so they never post one - checked against the existing refusal test in `inverted_post`.\n- One wording table: `machine::inverted_motion` (X left, Y toward the front, Z down) / `inverted_axis_line`.\n- Machine editor already shows the per-axis direction (#373); unchanged.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/375-show-inverted-axis.md`.\n\n## Readings\n- Golden diffs are exactly one added line each: `fanuc_x.nc` and `haas_x.nc` gain `(MACHINE X+ MOVES LEFT - INVERTED AXIS)` after line 2. No other golden changed (standard machines byte-identical).\n- `axis_direction::an_inverted_x_machine_posts_the_mirrored_program` now asserts the one header note and compares the rest line by line as before.\n- The RS-274 reader in `inverted_equivalence` ignores the comment (suite green).\n\n## Pinning tests\n- app `inverted_axis_display`: `the_setup_sheet_states_each_inverted_axis`, `a_standard_machine_adds_no_sheet_line`, `the_sheet_reads_the_machine_its_own_setup_mounts`, `the_header_states_the_inverted_axis_for_every_translating_post`, `one_wording_table_for_every_display`\n- ui lib `axis_note_tests`: `an_inverted_axis_is_noted_beside_its_triad_letter` (letter kept, note under it in the axis colour, arrows identical to a standard machine's), `a_standard_machine_adds_no_triad_label`\n- goldens `inverted_post::inverted_x_goldens_for_fanuc_and_haas`\n\n## Gate (debug, worktree target)\napp: setup_sheet 7, inverted_post 15, inverted_equivalence 2, axis_direction 12, posting 17, golden_cl 23, conformance 6, inverted_axis_display 5, machine 32, fanuc_post 8, tormach_post 4, post_not_judged 10 - all green. camcraft-post all suites green. camcraft-ui --lib (CWD crates/ui) 305 passed, 2 ignored, no snapshot change. clippy -D warnings on post/app/ui --all-targets clean.\n\nNot exercised: the GUI by hand (the triad note placement is a fixed uv drop under the letter; tested by position, not by eye).\n\nChangelog: An inverted machine axis is shown on the viewport triad, as a MACHINE AXES line on the setup sheet, and as a header comment in Fanuc/Haas programs\n\nFixes #375\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
